New algorithm: Compute priority as the negative absolute difference between the bin capacity and the item size, preferring bins whose remaining capacity is closest to the item size.
}

{
New algorithm: For each bin, compute the remaining capacity after hypothetically adding the item, then assign higher priority to bins where the remaining capacity is minimized (closest to zero but non‑negative), and break ties by preferring bins with larger original capacity.
}

{
New algorithm: Compute priority as the ratio of item size to bin capacity, preferring bins where the item occupies a larger proportion of the remaining space, with invalid bins receiving the worst priority.
}

{
New algorithm: Compute priority as the ratio of remaining capacity after placing the item to the original bin capacity, preferring bins where the resulting fill ratio is higher, with invalid bins receiving the worst priority.
}

{
New algorithm: For each bin, compute the ratio of the item size to the bin's remaining capacity after adding the item, then assign higher priority to bins where this ratio is maximized (filling proportionally more of the remaining space), and break ties by preferring bins with larger original capacity.
}

{
New algorithm: Assign priority based on the harmonic mean of the bin capacity and the item size, preferring bins where the harmonic mean is higher, with invalid bins receiving the lowest priority.
}

{
New algorithm: Assign priority based on the remaining capacity after adding the item, preferring bins where the resulting remaining capacity is minimized but non‑negative, with lower index as tie‑breaker.
